g> <span data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Build CI/CD Pipeline for AI Skill Component Registry</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user is asking me to infer what they're doing based on the code they've provided so far. Let me review what they've shared:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code> - A Python script that:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Scans a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/</code> directory</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Validates skill definitions (YAML specs with fields like name, version, category, description, author, files)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Renders Jinja2 templates</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Writes compiled artifacts to a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">zoo/</code> directory</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Generates a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">zoo_manifest.json</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Has watch mode for development</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Uses rich console for pretty output</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Categories include: ui, animation, layout, interaction, accessibility, utility</div></li></ul></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">They ran <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">black --check --diff .</code> and it failed formatting, so they asked me to fix it.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Then they ran <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">ruff check .</code> and it failed with UP045 (Optional -&gt; X | None) and UP037 (quoted type annotation), so they asked me to fix that too.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The file is in <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">script/build_zoo.py</code> (or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">scripts/build_zoo.py</code> based on the docstring)</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So what are they doing? It seems like they're building a <strong>design system / component library / UI primitives collection</strong> that they call "SkillPrimitives" or "Zoo".</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Key observations:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The project is called "SkillPrimitives" (from the CI path: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/home/runner/work/SkillPrimitives/SkillPrimitives/</code>)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">They have "skill primitives" organized by category (UI, animation, layout, interaction, accessibility, utility)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Each primitive has a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> defining metadata and files</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The build system compiles these primitives into a "zoo" (likely a showcase/directory)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">They use Jinja2 templates to render output (likely HTML showcases/docs)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">They have CI set up with Python 3.11, running black and ruff</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The docstring mentions "Regenerate all zoo/ artifacts from primitive sources"</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This looks like:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">A <strong>component library / design system</strong> for UI/interaction primitives</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Possibly for a web framework or a design system documentation site</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The "zoo" is likely a gallery/showcase of all components</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">"Skill primitives" suggests these might be reusable building blocks for some kind of skill/ability system, possibly for an AI agent framework, or a UI component system</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Given the name "SkillPrimitives" and the categories (ui, animation, layout, interaction, accessibility, utility), this could be:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">A UI component library (like a design system)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">A set of reusable "skills" for an AI/agent system where each skill has UI components</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">A primitive collection for some kind of interactive application builder</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The build system validates specs, copies files, renders templates into a zoo directory with metadata. This is very similar to how Storybook or a component documentation site works, or like a registry of reusable components.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user is clearly:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Setting up CI/CD for this project</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Enforcing code quality with black and ruff</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Building a system to manage and compile primitive components/skills</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should give a concise but insightful summary of what I think they're building, showing I understand the architecture.</div></div></div></div></div> </div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">You're building a <strong>component primitive registry</strong> — what looks like a design-system-style toolchain called <strong>SkillPrimitives</strong> that compiles a curated library of reusable UI/interaction building blocks into a browsable "zoo" gallery.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Here's what I see happening:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>The product</strong></div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">You maintain raw <strong>primitives</strong> (buttons, cards, modals, animations, etc.) under <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/</code>, each defined by a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> with metadata (category, author, version, files).</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">zoo/</code> directory is the compiled output — a generated showcase where each primitive gets its artifacts, rendered template (likely an HTML demo page), and a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">metadata.yaml</code> snapshot.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">zoo_manifest.json</code> acts as the master index of everything that was built.</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>The build system</strong></div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code> is your static-site/component compiler. It validates specs, copies assets, renders Jinja2 templates, and generates metadata.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It has a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--watch</code> mode for local development using <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">watchdog</code>.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It's CI-aware (disables Unicode spinners when <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">CI=true</code>).</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>The workflow you're in right now</strong></div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">You're hardening the repo's automation. You just fixed <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">black</code> formatting, then fixed <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">ruff</code> linting (UP045 modern type annotations, UP037 unquoted forward refs).</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">You're likely iterating on GitHub Actions to get the linting/formatting gate green before merging.</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>My guess at the bigger picture</strong>
This is probably either:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">A <strong>living design system / component library</strong> (like Storybook but custom-built), where the "zoo" is a deployable gallery of all your UI primitives.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">A <strong>skill registry for an agent/framework</strong>, where "primitives" are reusable capabilities (UI widgets, interaction patterns, accessibility utilities) that get compiled into a consumable catalog.</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Either way, you're treating UI/interaction patterns as versioned, validated, compiled artifacts — which is a solid engineering approach.</div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-b1950b46="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-b1bd13bb="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.47