ooking at the code logic, if <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.get("files")</code> returns a dict (because the YAML author wrote <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">files:</code> followed by dict keys without a hyphen), then iterating over the dict yields string keys. The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">isinstance(file_entry, str)</code> branch handles these keys as filenames. So the code would look for a file literally named "src" and fail with "Referenced file missing: src". It wouldn't crash with TypeError.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But what if <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.get("files")</code> returns <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">None</code>? Then <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.get("files", [])</code> returns <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">[]</code>, and the loop doesn't run. No error.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">What if <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec["files"]</code> is missing and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.get("files")</code> returns <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">None</code>? Same, default to <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">[]</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">What if the YAML has:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="