 194.773333 363.477333a317.781333 317.781333 0 0 0 99.285334 275.968 222.72 222.72 0 0 1 75.818666 162.346667v5.717333A131.328 131.328 0 0 0 501.077333 938.666667h22.016a131.328 131.328 0 0 0 131.2-131.2v-19.498667a189.269333 189.269333 0 0 1 68.693334-142.250667 319.744 319.744 0 0 0 2.218666-479.146666zM523.093333 867.584h-22.016a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117333-60.074667l-0.256-11.008h142.506667v11.008a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117334 60.074667z m152.917334-275.2A272.64 272.64 0 0 0 591.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Standardize Primitive Naming and Schema for Consistent Metadata</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user is asking which spec.yaml format (dict with "src" key vs bare string) is better for their NL-to-motion transformer project. I should think about what makes sense for a robotics skill primitive library where primitives might need to be composed, referenced, and potentially have multiple files or output artifacts.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The dict form (<code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">- src: base.py</code>) is more extensible because:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It allows adding <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">dest</code> key later if you want the output file to have a different name in the zoo</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It's consistent with how more complex primitives will look (e.g., a primitive that has multiple files or needs renaming)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It makes the schema uniform across all primitives - some might need dict entries, so having base use dict too keeps everything predictable</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For an NL-to-motion transformer, you might want metadata per file (like entry points, dependencies, etc.) and the dict form gives you room to add keys</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The string form is simpler but less future-proof.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should recommend the dict form but mention both work.</div></div></div></div></div> </div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For an NL-to-motion transformer, <strong>use the dict form</strong>:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9=