08h142.506667v11.008a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117334 60.074667z m152.917334-275.2A272.64 272.64 0 0 0 591.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Refining RobotState Class Validation Serialization Docstrings Type Hints Logging</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user wants a production-grade <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code> — the abstract base class for all manipulation primitives that the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__.py</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code> reference.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Given the context:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This is a robotics NL→motion transformer repo</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base</code> is the abstract base class for all manipulation primitives</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It should define the interface that all primitives implement</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It needs to be something the transformer can compose over</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It should be clean, typed, and production-grade</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Key things a robotics primitive base class should have:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Abstract method for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute()</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">run()</code> — the actual motion</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Abstract method for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate()</code> — check preconditions (kinematic feasibility, collision, etc.)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Metadata properties (name, version, category, description)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Parameter schema — what arguments does this primitive accept? (critical for NL→motion because the transformer needs to know what parameters to generate)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Maybe a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">to_trajectory()</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">to_motion_plan()</code> method</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Maybe <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">dependencies</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">preconditions</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Serialization support</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Context/robot interface — the primitive needs to know about the robot state</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me think about the interface carefully.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For an NL→motion system, the flow is typically:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">NL query → transformer → skill name + parameters</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Skill registry loads the primitive</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Primitive is instantiated with parameters</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Primitive validates preconditions</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Primitive executes (generates trajectory or sends commands to robot)</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So the base class should define:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">name</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">version</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">category</code> class attributes</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code> — JSON schema or similar describing what params this primitive accepts</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__(self, **params)</code> — initialize with parameters</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate(self, robot_state) -&gt; bool</code> — check if this primitive can run given current state</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute(self, robot_interface) -&gt; Trajectory | None</code> — run the primitive</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">to_dict()</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from_dict()</code> — serialization for composition/chaining</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking at the repo structure (annotate, compose, validate, demo), the primitives are likely:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Python classes that define motion skills</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code> labels demos with these primitives</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">compose</code> chains them</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> checks feasibility</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">demo</code> executes them</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So the base class should be something like:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" 