" class="chat-content-item chat-content-item-assistant" data-archer-id="19fefd1e-8382-8d57-8000-0ae660c36c04"><!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" data-v-b1950b46="" class="segment segment-assistant"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-avatar"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" class="avatar"><canvas data-v-b81624a4="" data-v-88be9e2e="" class="rive-container" width="154" height="154" style="width: 56px; height: 56px;"></canvas></div></div> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-container" dir="auto"> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content"><div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content-box"> <div data-v-004597db="" class="container-block"><div data-v-004597db="" class="block-item"><div data-v-56fb9f7a="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="toolcall-container thinking-container block-container" share-mode="false"><div data-v-bc9c95fe="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-title-container default"><div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name line"><svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-name-icon" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="k15"><path d="M725.205333 166.656A320 320 0 0 0 194.773333 363.477333a317.781333 317.781333 0 0 0 99.285334 275.968 222.72 222.72 0 0 1 75.818666 162.346667v5.717333A131.328 131.328 0 0 0 501.077333 938.666667h22.016a131.328 131.328 0 0 0 131.2-131.2v-19.498667a189.269333 189.269333 0 0 1 68.693334-142.250667 319.744 319.744 0 0 0 2.218666-479.146666zM523.093333 867.584h-22.016a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117333-60.074667l-0.256-11.008h142.506667v11.008a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117334 60.074667z m152.917334-275.2A272.64 272.64 0 0 0 591.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Create grasp package __init__ and provide corrected base.py</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user has shared a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> primitive implementation. It inherits from <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> (the base class I generated earlier), but there are issues:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The base class I generated has abstract methods <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate(self, state: RobotState) -&gt; bool</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute(self, robot_interface: Any) -&gt; Trajectory</code>. But this <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> class defines <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate(self, segment: dict[str, Any]) -&gt; bool</code> with a completely different signature, and defines <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code> instead of <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code>.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> class doesn't define the class-level metadata attributes (<code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">version</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">category</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">description</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">author</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code>).</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> method seems to be for annotation/demonstration segmentation (finding grasp events in recorded trajectories), not for execution.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user said they have files like <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">compose</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">demo</code>. This <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> class seems designed for the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code> pipeline (detecting segments from demonstrations), not the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code> pipeline.</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This reveals a mismatch between the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> base class I designed (which was execution-oriented) and what the user actually needs. The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> base class should probably support both:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate_segment</code> for the annotation pipeline</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code> for the demo/execution pipeline</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or perhaps there are two different base classes: one for annotation/detectors and one for executors. But given the user's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code> description ("Abstract base class for all manipulation primitives"), it seems like <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> should be the single base class that supports both annotation and execution concerns.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me reconsider the architecture based on this new information:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user has:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code> - labels human demonstrations or motion segments with natural language</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">compose</code> - sequences or blends skill primitives into full behaviors</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> - checks composed skill chains</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">demo</code> - executes or visualizes motion</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code> - builds the zoo</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> base class needs to support:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Annotation/Detection</strong>: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect(gripper, state, velocity) -&gt; segments</code> - finds where this primitive occurs in a demonstration</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Description</strong>: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe(segment) -&gt; str</code> - generates natural language description for a detected segment</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Validation</strong>: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate(state) -&gt; bool</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate_segment(segment) -&gt; bool</code> - checks if a segment is valid</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Execution</strong>: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute(robot_interface) -&gt; Trajectory</code> - runs the primitive</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> implementation shows:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> for finding grasp events in recorded data</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> that takes a segment dict (for annotation validation)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code> for NL generation</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But it doesn't have <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code>. That's fine - maybe not all primitives implement execution yet, or maybe <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> is an annotation primitive.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should update the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code> to accommodate this actual usage pattern. The base class should:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Keep <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code> as abstract OR provide a default that raises NotImplementedError</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Add <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate_segment</code> methods with sensible defaults</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Keep class-level metadata</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking at the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> class more carefully:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It imports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.base import Primitive</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This means the package structure is <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives/primitives/base/__init__.py</code> which exports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> primitive lives somewhere else, probably <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives/primitives/grasp/grasp.py</code></div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> class overrides <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> with a different signature than what I put in <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code>. This will cause a runtime error if <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code> enforces the abstract method signature. In Python, abstract methods only enforce existence, not exact signature, but if someone calls <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp.validate(state)</code> expecting a RobotState but gets a dict, it will crash.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I need to redesign <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code> to match the actual interface the user is implementing. Let me look at what methods the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> class actually implements:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect(gripper, state, velocity) -&gt; list[dict]</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate(segment) -&gt; bool</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe(segment) -&gt; str</code></div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">And what the base class should probably require:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Class metadata: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">name</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">version</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">category</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">description</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">author</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> - for annotation</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code> - for NL generation</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> - could be overloaded for both segment validation and state validation, or we need separate methods</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code> - for demo</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Given that <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> is used differently in <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> (takes a segment dict) vs what I designed (takes a RobotState), I should probably rename the state-validation method to something else, or make <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> accept either. But the cleanest approach is:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-