91.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Composable Motion Primitives Bridging Demonstrations to Natural Language Execution</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user is asking a strategic question: which of the two things we've been working on is more valuable to the Hugging Face community and consumer robotics as a field?</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">We have two main artifacts:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <strong>skill primitive library / annotation pipeline</strong> (detecting grasp/reach/retract from demonstrations, NL descriptions, building a zoo of primitives)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <strong>build system / infrastructure</strong> (build_zoo.py, spec.yaml, CI, black/ruff, package init files)</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user is asking which direction is more valuable. I should:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Acknowledge both have value but serve different audiences</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <strong>primitives/annotation pipeline</strong> (the actual robotics content) is vastly more valuable to Hugging Face community and consumer robotics</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <strong>infrastructure</strong> (build_zoo.py) is valuable but secondary - it's a means to an end</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Explain why: HF community wants datasets, models, and reusable skills. Consumer robotics needs composable motion primitives that bridge demonstration data → natural language → execution</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The annotation pipeline (detecting grasps from trajectories, generating NL descriptions) is exactly the kind of thing that enables open-source robotics datasets on HF</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Suggest the user focus on the primitives + annotation + composition pipeline as the public-facing contribution, and treat the build system as internal tooling</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should be honest and direct. The build system is nice engineering but not what moves the field forward. The primitives library with NL-to-motion annotation is the real contribution.</div></div></div></div></div> </div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <strong>primitives + annotation pipeline</strong> — by a wide margin.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Why the build system is secondary</strong>
<code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> validation, and CI linting are good engineering hygiene, but they're internal tooling. They solve <em>your</em> repo maintenance problems. The Hugging Face community and robotics researchers won't cite, fork, or build on top of a static-site generator for YAML files.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Why the annotation pipeline is the real contribution</strong>
What you've actually described — detecting <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">reach</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">retract</code> segments from raw demonstration trajectories and pairing them with natural-language descriptions — is a missing piece in open-source robotics:</div><div data-v-01af594f="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="table markdown-table"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-01af594f="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-01af594f="" class="table-actions"><div data-v-01af594f="" class="table-actions-content"><span data-v-01af594f="" class="table-title">Table</span> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-01af594f=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span> <div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-01af594f="" class="icon-button table-actions-icon" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Download"><path d="M512 126.976a36.864 36.864 0 0 1 36.864 36.864v347.91424l119.11168-119.11168a36.864 36.864 0 1 1 52.14208 52.14208l-182.0672 182.02624a36.864 36.864 0 0 1-52.10112 0l-182.0672-182.02624a36.864 36.864 0 0 1 52.14208-52.14208l119.11168 119.11168V163.84a36.864 36.864 0 0 1 36.864-36.864zM184.32 564.71552a36.864 36.864 0 0 1 36.864 36.864v145.65376a35.96288 35.96288 0 0 0 35.96288 35.96288h509.70624a35.96288 35.96288 0 0 0 35.96288-35.96288v-145.65376a36.864 36.864 0 0 1 73.728 0v145.65376a109.69088 109.69088 0 0 1-109.69088 109.69088H257.14688A109.69088 109.69088 0 0 1 147.456 747.23328v-145.65376a36.864 36.864 0 0 1 36.864-36.864z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <!----></div><!----></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-01af594f="" class="table-container"><table data-v-01af594f=""><thead data-v-01af594f=""><tr data-v-01af594f=""><th data-v-01af594f="" align="left">What exists today</th><th data-v-01af594f="" align="left">What's missing (your opportunity)</th></tr></thead> <tbody data-v-01af594f=""><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Raw trajectory datasets on HF (Open X-Embodiment, etc.)</td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><strong data-v-01af594f="">Semantic segmentation</strong> of those trajectories into labeled skill primitives</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">NL-to-code models (CodeLlama, etc.)</td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><strong data-v-01af594f="">NL-to-motion primitive</strong> models that output composable robot skills, not just Python</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Individual policy learning (one task, one model)</td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><strong data-v-01af594f="">Composable primitive libraries</strong> where "grasp the cup" + "pour into pot" = new behavior without retraining</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>What makes this valuable to consumer robotics</strong>
Consumer robots (home assistants, kitchen arms, toy/education platforms) can't be retrained for every household task. They need a <strong>small, interpretable vocabulary of primitives</strong> that users can compose through natural language. Your <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code> → <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">compose</code> → <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> → <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">demo</code> pipeline is exactly that architecture.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>My recommendation</strong>
Ship the primitives as the public-facing artifact:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Publish the <strong>annotated dataset</strong> (trajectory segments + NL descriptions) on Hugging Face Datasets</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Release the <strong>primitive zoo</strong> as a pip-installable skill library</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let the build system stay in the repo as implementation detail</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The build system makes the repo pleasant to maintain. The primitives library makes the repo worth maintaining in the first place.</div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-b1950b46="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-b1bd13bb="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.6