n: given detected primitives [grasp, pour, release], compose them into a full task description. Or it could mean composing motion trajectories.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But the user said "we are building a annotation engine" — that's the clarifying statement. So I should optimize base.py for annotation. If execution comes later, they can add a separate mixin or subclass.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me design the clean annotation-engine base.py:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Key principles:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Single responsibility</strong>: annotation only. No execution baggage.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Stateless-friendly</strong>: primitives like <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> don't need <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__</code> parameters.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Batch-friendly</strong>: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> takes arrays, returns lists of segments.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Pipeline method</strong>: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate()</code> runs the full pipeline for convenience.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Metadata</strong>: class-level metadata for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code> and manifest generation.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>No numpy import in base?</strong> The user's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> imports numpy. The base class signature should use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">np.ndarray</code>. That's fine.</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, s