        <span class="token keyword">if</span> self<span class="token punctuation">.</span>validate<span class="token punctuation">(</span>seg<span class="token punctuation">)</span>
    <span class="token punctuation">]</span></code></pre></div></div> <div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This is useful for the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code> script.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Now, what about metadata for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code>? The user wants <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">get_metadata()</code> to auto-generate spec.yaml. For an annotation engine, the metadata might also include what signals the primitive uses (gripper, state, velocity).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me also think about whether <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> should inherit from <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">ABC</code>. Yes, because <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> is abstract.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Should there be a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code>? The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> doesn't use parameters. But future primitives might (e.g., <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">threshold</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">window_size</code>). It's harmless to keep as a classvar with empty default.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking at the user's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp.detect</code>, it has hardcoded values like <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">0.5</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">0.6</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">0.92</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">0.75</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">3</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">5</code>. These could be parameters. But the user didn't make them configurable. So for now, parameters are optional.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me think about whether the base class needs <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__</code>. Since <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> doesn't override it, the base class can have a simple <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__</code> that does nothing, or no <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__</code> at all. Python classes don't need explicit <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But if we want to support parameters later, a default <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__(self, **kwargs)</code> that stores them as <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">self.config</code> might be nice. But it's not necessary for the annotation engine.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, I think the cleanest approach is:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""