-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">RobotState</code> dataclass</td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Execution-time precondition checking — not needed for annotation</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Trajectory</code> dataclass</td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Execution output — not needed for annotation</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate_state()</code></td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Runtime safety check for real robots — irrelevant here</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute()</code></td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Motion generation — out of scope for an annotation engine</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_validate_and_coerce()</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code></td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Your <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> is stateless; parameters can be added later when needed</td></tr><tr data-v-01af594f=""><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from_parameters()</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">to_dict()</code> / <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from_dict()</code></td><td data-v-01af594f="" align="left">Serialization for motion composition — not for annotation</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>What I kept (and added):</strong></div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> as the sole <strong>abstract method</strong> — every primitive must know how to find itself in raw data</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code> with <strong>sensible defaults</strong> — your <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> can skip overriding <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> if the type check is all it needs</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate()</code></strong> — a new convenience method that runs <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect → validate → describe</code> in one shot. This is exactly what your <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate</code> script will call</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">get_metadata()</code> — still there so <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">build_zoo.py</code> can auto-generate <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> entries</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Your <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code> now slots in with zero friction — no unused inherited methods, no forced <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__</code> calls, no <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">NotImplementedError</code> traps.</div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!