lass="paragraph" dir="auto">The user wants to know if spec.yaml and <strong>init</strong>.py need to change based on the new annotation-focused base.py I just provided.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me think about what changed in base.py:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Removed <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">RobotState</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Trajectory</code> dataclasses</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Removed <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate_state</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">execute</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_validate_and_coerce</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from_parameters</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">to_dict</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from_dict</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Kept <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect</code> (abstract), <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> (concrete), <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe</code> (concrete)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Added <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">annotate()</code> convenience method</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Kept <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">get_metadata()</code> but it no longer includes <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code></div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Now, for the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__.py</code> in the base folder:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Previously it exported <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">RobotState</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Trajectory</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Now it should only export <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> since the other two are gone</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Should it export anything else? The base.py only has <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">logger</code> now. So <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__.py</code> should just export <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive</code>.</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code>:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">files</code> field references <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The metadata fields (name, version, category, description, author) are still valid</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">parameters_schema</code> is no longer in <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">get_metadata()</code>, but that doesn't affect spec.yaml since spec.yaml is the source of truth for build_zoo.py, not the other way around</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The category <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base</code> is still in VALID_CATEGORIES</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So the changes needed:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base/__init__.py</code> - remove <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">RobotState</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Trajectory</code> from exports</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> - no changes needed, it's fine as-is</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, let me also consider: should <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> include anything about the annotation interface? Like <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">supports_annotation: true</code>? The user didn't ask for that, and the current build system doesn't have a field for it. So no change needed there.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user asked "does spec.yaml and <strong>init</strong>.py need to change" - so I should answer clearly: spec.yaml stays the same, <strong>init</strong>.py needs to drop the removed exports.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me provide the updated <strong>init</strong>.py content.</div></div></div></div></div> </div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Yes — only <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">__init__.py</code> needs a small update. <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code> is fine as-is.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">spec.yaml</code></strong> — no changes. It already describes the primitive correctly:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">yaml</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-