 class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user wants me to reorganize imports in the grasp.py file to pass ruff lint checks. The main issues are likely:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Import order: stdlib first, then third-party, then local</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from __future__ import annotations</code> should be at the top</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">typing.Any</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">typing.ClassVar</code> - these should use modern annotations or be properly ordered</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The import <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from base import Primitive</code> - this is a relative import that ruff might flag</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me check the current imports:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-python"><code class="language-python"><span class="token keyword">from</span> __future__ <span class="token keyword">import</span> annotations

<span class="token keyword">from</span> typing <span class="token keyword">import</span> Any<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ClassVar

<span class="token keyword">import</span> numpy <span class="token keyword">as</span> np

<span class="token keyword">from</span> base <span class="token keyword">import</span> Primitive</code></pre></div></div> <div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Issues:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from typing import Any, ClassVar</code> - ruff might prefer <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">typing</code> imports to be in a specific section, or might want us to use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">typing</code> module directly</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from base import Primitive</code> - this is a relative import without explicit relative syntax. Ruff might want <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from .base import Primitive</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.base import Primitive</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Import ordering: stdlib (<code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">typing</code>), third-party (<code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">numpy</code>), local (<code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base</code>)</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking at ruff rules:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I001: unsorted-imports</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I002: missing-required-import (usually <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from __future__ import annotations</code>)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">TID252: relative-imports-from-parent</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from base import Primitive</code> is likely problematic because it's an implicit relative import. In a package structure like <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives/primitives/grasp/grasp.py</code>, importing <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from base</code> would try to import from <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives/primitives/base/</code>. Ruff's TID252 or similar rules might flag this.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Better to use absolute imports: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.base import Primitive</code></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, but looking at the user's project structure, the base primitive is at <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives/primitives/base/</code>. So from <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp.py</code>, the absolute import would be <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.base import Primitive</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">However, if the user wants it to work when run directly too, they might prefer relative: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from ..base import Primitive</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from ...primitives.base import Primitive</code> - but that's messy.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking at the user's Grasp class draft, they had:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style