e> returns <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Any</code> because <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">segment</code> is typed as <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">dict[str, Any]</code>, so mypy complains about <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">no-any-return</code> on the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate</code> method which is declared to return <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">bool</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The fix is to explicitly annotate or cast the confidence value to <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">float</code>. I should use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">confidence: float = segment.get("confidence", 0.0)</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">confidence = float(segment.get("confidence", 0.0))</code>. The latter is safer at runtime too.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me regenerate the full file with this fix applied, keeping all the ruff-clean imports and formatting intact.</div></div></div></div></div> </div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"></div></div><div data-v-004597db="" class="container-block"><div data-v-004597db="" class="block-item"><div data-v-d664c8c3=""><div data-v-863d6f1b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="toolcall-container default toolcall-ipython"><div data-v-bc9c95fe="" data-v-863d6f1b="" class="toolcall-title-container default"><div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name line"><svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-name-icon" width="1em