38.186667-42.410667 40.021333l-17.194667 1.706667c-173.994667 20.949333-253.824 136.405333-253.824 304.554667 86.997333-89.557333 163.925333-105.386667 270.933334-107.861334a42.026667 42.026667 0 0 1 42.752 42.24v125.226667c0 34.56 38.272 53.845333 65.706666 35.925333l5.376-4.096 304.426667-272.213333a42.666667 42.666667 0 0 0 2.986667-60.714667l-3.413334-3.285333-304.469333-264.277333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Share</span></div> <!----></div> <!----></div>   <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div></div></div></div><div data-v-b1950b46="" class="chat-content-item chat-content-item-assistant" data-archer-id="19ff0141-3192-8bae-8000-0ae64990f538"><!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" data-v-b1950b46="" class="segment segment-assistant"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-avatar"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" class="avatar"><canvas data-v-b81624a4="" data-v-88be9e2e="" class="rive-container" width="154" height="154" style="width: 56px; height: 56px;"></canvas></div></div> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-container" dir="auto"> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content"><div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content-box"> <div data-v-004597db="" class="container-block"><div data-v-004597db="" class="block-item"><div data-v-56fb9f7a="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="toolcall-container thinking-container block-container" share-mode="false"><div data-v-bc9c95fe="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-title-container default"><div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name line"><svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-name-icon" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="k15"><path d="M725.205333 166.656A320 320 0 0 0 194.773333 363.477333a317.781333 317.781333 0 0 0 99.285334 275.968 222.72 222.72 0 0 1 75.818666 162.346667v5.717333A131.328 131.328 0 0 0 501.077333 938.666667h22.016a131.328 131.328 0 0 0 131.2-131.2v-19.498667a189.269333 189.269333 0 0 1 68.693334-142.250667 319.744 319.744 0 0 0 2.218666-479.146666zM523.093333 867.584h-22.016a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117333-60.074667l-0.256-11.008h142.506667v11.008a60.16 60.16 0 0 1-60.117334 60.074667z m152.917334-275.2A272.64 272.64 0 0 0 591.957333 725.333333h-44.330666v-255.445333a106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333-100.096 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 35.584 35.584 0 0 1-71.082667 0 35.584 35.584 0 1 0-71.125333 0 106.666667 106.666667 0 0 0 71.125333 100.096V725.333333h-47.018667a307.029333 307.029333 0 0 0-87.04-137.984 248.874667 248.874667 0 0 1 169.941334-430.933333 246.101333 246.101333 0 0 1 165.376 63.232 248.661333 248.661333 0 0 1-1.706667 372.693333h-0.085333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-name-text">Detect Z Rise Using Position Difference Ensuring Monotonicity</span></div> <!----> <div data-v-bc9c95fe="" class="toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg data-v-bc9c95fe="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Right_b"><path d="M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user wants a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">lift.py</code> primitive following the same pattern as <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp.py</code>. Lift is a manipulation primitive where the end effector moves upward after a grasp. For annotation purposes, I should detect it from state/velocity data — typically a vertical (Z-axis) displacement after a grasp event.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me think about the detection logic:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Lift typically follows a grasp</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It involves upward movement of the end effector (positive Z displacement)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Could be detected from gripper state (already closed) + upward Z velocity/position change</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or from state array where Z coordinate increases significantly</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I'll model it similarly to Grasp:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">detect(gripper, state, velocity)</code> — find lift segments</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">validate(segment)</code> — check quality</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">describe(segment)</code> — NL description</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For detection:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Lift is characterized by the end effector moving upward while the gripper is closed</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">We can look for periods where gripper is closed (&lt; 0.5) and the Z position increases by some threshold</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or look at velocity: positive Z velocity while gripper closed</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Since <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">state</code> is a 2-D array, I'll assume state[:, 2] or similar is the Z position. But I don't know the exact state format. Let me make it general — I'll use the Z component and look for upward displacement.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking at the Grasp primitive, it only uses <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">gripper</code>. For Lift, I should use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">state</code> (end effector position). Let me assume <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">state</code> has shape (timesteps, n_features) and the Z position is at some index. I'll make the Z index configurable or just look at the last 3 columns as XYZ.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me design it:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Gripper must be closed (&lt; CLOSED_THRESHOLD) for the duration</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Z position must increase by at least some threshold over the segment</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Segment should have a minimum duration</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Detection approach:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Find regions where gripper is continuously closed</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Within those regions, find where Z increases monotonically or significantly</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Extract the segment</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or simpler:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Look for transitions where Z starts increasing while gripper is closed</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The segment spans from the start of upward motion until Z stabilizes or gripper opens</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me keep it practical and similar to Grasp's style. I'll detect lift as a period where:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Gripper is closed (to ensure we're holding something)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Z position increases by at least Z_RISE_THRESHOLD</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Minimum duration</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I'll iterate through timesteps, and when I find a closed gripper with sufficient Z rise over a window, I mark it.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">For the state array, I'll assume the Z position is <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">state[:, 2]</code> (3rd column, 0-indexed). This is a reasonable assumption for XYZ position data.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me write it:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-python"><code class="language-python"><span class="token triple-quoted-string string">"""lift.py — Vertical lift primitive after object acquisition.

Detects lift events from demonstration trajectories by identifying
upward end-effector motion while the gripper remains closed.
"""</span>

<span class="token keyword">from</span> __future__ <span class="token keyword">import</span> annotations

<span class="token keyword">from</span> typing <span class="token keyword">import</span> Any<span class="token punctuation">,</span> ClassVar

<span class="token keyword">import</span> numpy <span class="token keyword">as</span> np

<span class="token keyword">from</span> skill_primitives<span class="token punctuation">.</span>primitives<span class="token punctuation">.</span>base <span class="token keyword">import</span> Primitive


<span class="token keyword">class</span> <span class="token class-name">Lift</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>Primitive<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>
    <span class="token triple-quoted-string string">"""Lift the grasped object vertically.

    Detected from sustained upward Z displacement while the gripper
    remains closed.
    """</span>

    name<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">"lift"</span>
    version<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">"0.1.0"</span>
    category<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">"manipulation"</span>
    description<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">"Lift the grasped object vertically."</span>
    author<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token string">"ksaad20"</span>

    <span class="token comment"># Detection hyperparameters</span>
    CLOSED_THRESHOLD<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">float</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">0.5</span>
    Z_RISE_THRESHOLD<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">float</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">0.02</span>  <span class="token comment"># meters</span>
    MIN_DURATION<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">int</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">5</span>
    Z_INDEX<span class="token punctuation">:</span> ClassVar<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">int</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">2</span>  <span class="token comment"># Z position in state array</span>

    <span class="token keyword">def</span> <span class="token function">detect</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>
        self<span class="token punctuation">,</span>
        gripper<span class="token punctuation">:</span> np<span class="token punctuation">.</span>ndarray<span class="token punctuation">,</span>
        state<span class="token punctuation">:</span> np<span class="token punctuation">.</span>ndarray <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token boolean">None</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token boolean">None</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
        velocity<span class="token punctuation">:</span> np<span class="token punctuation">.</span>ndarray <span class="token operator">|</span> <span class="token boolean">None</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token boolean">None</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">-</span><span class="token operator">&gt;</span> <span class="token builtin">list</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">dict</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> Any<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>
        segments<span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token builtin">list</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">dict</span><span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> Any<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span>
        <span class="token keyword">if</span> state <span class="token keyword">is</span> <span class="token boolean">None</span> <span class="token keyword">or</span> <span class="token builtin">len</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>gripper<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">&lt;</span> <span class="token number">2</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span>
            <span class="token keyword">return</span> segments

        n <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token builtin">len</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>gripper<span class="token punctuation">)</span>
        z <span class="token operator">=</span> state<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> self<span class="token punctuation">.</span>Z_INDEX<span class="token punctuation">]</span>

        t <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">0</span>
        <span class="token keyword">while</span> t <span class="token operator">&lt;</span> n<span class="token punctuation">:</span>
            <span class="token comment"># Find start: gripper closed and beginning of rise</span>
            <span class="token keyword">if</span> gripper<span class="token punctuation">[</span>t<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">&gt;=</span> self<span class="token punctuation">.</span>CLOSED_THRESHOLD<span class="token punctuation">:</span>
                t <span class="token operator">+=</span> <span class="token number">1</span>
                <span class="token keyword">continue</span>

            <span class="token comment"># Look ahead for sufficient Z rise while gripper stays closed</span>
            start <span class="token operator">=</span> t
            z_start <span class="token operator">=</span> z<span class="token punctuation">[</span>t<span class="token punctuation">]</span>
            t <span class="token operator">+=</span> <span class="token number">1</span>
            <span class="token keyword">while</span> t <span class="token operator">&lt;</span> n <span class="token keyword">and</span> gripper<span class="token punctuation">[</span>t<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">&lt;</span> self<span class="token punctuation">.</span>CLOSED_THRESHOLD<span class="token punctuation">:</span>
                <span class="token keyword">if</span> z<span class="token punctuation">[</span>t<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">-</span> z_start <span class="token operator">&gt;=</span> self<span class="token punctuation">.</span>Z_RISE_THRESHOLD <span class="token keyword">and</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>t <span class="token operator">-</span> start<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">&gt;=</span> self<span class="token punctuation">.</span>MIN_DURATION<span class="token punctuation">:</span>
                    <span class="token comment"># Found a lift segment; extend to peak or gripper open</span>
                    end <span class="token operator">=</span> t
