0096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-9445e104="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="toolcall-content"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="resize-container" style="height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-9445e104="" class="slot-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-56fb9f7a="" class="markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user just got a mypy error on reach.py. I fixed it by adding explicit <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">speed: np.ndarray = np.linalg.norm(...)</code> type annotations on the local variables before returning them. This resolves the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">no-any-return</code> error because mypy now knows the return type is <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">np.ndarray</code> rather than <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Any</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should present the fixed file clearly.</div></div></div></div></div> </div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">plain</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d8