        <span class="token keyword">raise</span> ValueError<span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string-interpolation"><span class="token string">f"Primitive class </span><span class="token interpolation"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>cls<span class="token punctuation">.</span>__name__<span class="token punctuation">}</span></span><span class="token string"> must have a 'name' attribute"</span></span><span class="token punctuation">)</span>
    _PRIMITIVES<span class="token punctuation">[</span>cls<span class="token punctuation">.</span>name<span class="token punctuation">]</span> <span class="token operator">=</span> cls
    <span class="token keyword">return</span> cls</code></pre></div></div> <div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, but if <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> is imported by <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code>, and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> calls <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_discover()</code> which imports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives.primitives</code>, that's a circular import because <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code> is still being executed.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">To avoid this, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_discover()</code> should not import <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">skill_primitives.primitives</code>. Instead, it should use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">importlib</code> to import the base module and then scan submodules by constructing import paths directly.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, even simpler: since <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code> imports all the primitive modules before importing <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code>, by the time <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> is imported, all the primitive modules are already in <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">sys.modules</code>. So <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_discover()</code> can just look at what's already imported.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But that's fragile. What if someone imports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> directly without going through <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code>?</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Better approach: lazy discovery that doesn't rely on <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code> having already imported everything. Use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">pkgutil</code> with the package path from the filesystem.</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.