67v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-python"><code class="language-python"><span class="token keyword">from</span> skill_primitives<span class="token punctuation">.</span>primitives<span class="token punctuation">.</span>grasp <span class="token keyword">import</span> Grasp  <span class="token comment"># noqa: F401</span>
<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token punctuation">.</span></code></pre></div></div> <div class="paragraph" dir="auto">These are explicit imports. If they keep these, then when <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> is imported, all the primitive classes are already loaded in memory. The registry just needs to collect them.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But the user didn't include the auto-discovery in their draft. They just have empty <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_PRIMITIVES</code> and the registration functions. So maybe they want me to complete it by adding the auto-registration of the imported classes?</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, looking at the imports with <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">noqa: F401</code>, these imports are in <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> itself. So <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> imports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Grasp</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Lift</code>, etc. But then it doesn't do anything with them. The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_PRIMITIVES</code> dict stays empty.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I think the user wants me to either:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Add code that registers those imported classes automatically</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or replace the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">noqa: F401</code> imports with actual registration calls</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or add auto-discovery</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The cleanest production approach is auto-discovery. Let me provide that. But I need to handle the circular import carefully.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, I just realized: the user's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code> imports from <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code>. And <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> would need to import the primitive classes to register them. This is a circular dependency.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The standard way to solve this is:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> defines the registration functions and the dict, but does NOT import primitives</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code> imports all primitives, then imports from <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code>, then calls a discovery function or manually registers them</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Each primitive file calls <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">register_primitive</code> as a class decorator</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> doesn't need to import anything</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But the primitive files I generated don't have the decorator. Adding it would require regenerating all of them.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Another approach: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> uses lazy auto-discovery. When <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">get_primitive</code> is called, it scans the package. This avoids circular imports because the scanning happens at runtime, not at import time.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me go with the lazy auto-discovery approach. It's the most robust.</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip t