asp.py</code> imports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base</code>, not <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry</code>. So:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> → <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp/__init__.py</code> → <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp.py</code> → <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">base.py</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">No cycle back to <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code></div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code> imports <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code>. So when Python starts loading <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">primitives/__init__.py</code>:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It hits <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.base import Primitive</code> — loads base</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It hits <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.grasp import Grasp</code> — loads grasp</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">... loads all primitives ...</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It hits <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.registry import ...</code> — starts loading registry</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code> tries to import <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">from skill_primitives.primitives.grasp import Grasp</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grasp</code> is already fully loaded (step 2), so this is just a module cache lookup</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So there's no circular import problem! The primitives are loaded before registry, and registry just re-imports them from cache.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Great, so explicit registration works fine.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me write the production-grade <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">registry.py</code>:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">Python</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></pa