s="paragraph" dir="auto">But wait, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">Primitive.name</code> is defined as <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">ClassVar[str] = ""</code>. So mypy knows it's a string. But <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">not cls.name</code> is fine.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, there's a subtle issue: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_PRIMITIVES: dict[str, type[Primitive]] = {}</code> and then <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_PRIMITIVES[_cls.name] = _cls</code>. Since <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_cls</code> is inferred as <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">type[Primitive]</code> from the tuple, this should be fine.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">One more thing: I should make sure <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">register_primitive</code> accepts <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">type[Primitive]</code> properly. The user's draft had <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">cls: type[Primitive]</code>. That's correct.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me also consider if the user wants auto-discovery capability. I can add a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">_discover()</code> function as a bonus, but keep the explicit registration as the primary mechanism. Or I can just provide the explicit version since it's cleaner and matches their draft exactly.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, I realize the user might want the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">noqa: F401</code> imports because they want the registry to expose those classes without using them directly